    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0717" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.248/222: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-05T21:00:00+03:00">July 5, 1942—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 5—8:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>243. For the President. One of the items on the list submitted to the Harriman
                    Mission in September [1941] by the Soviet Naval authorities was a request for
                    PBY Navy planes. These planes could not be spared at that time. The Navy
                        Commissar<anchor n="9" xml:id="d593-f1"/> now informs me that he has again
                    requested 60 PBY planes for use in the Vladivostok and Murmansk–Archangel areas,
                    and I am convinced that if these <pb facs="0718" n="712" xml:id="pg712"/> planes
                    could be spared they would be of great value in protecting convoys in those
                    areas and thus prevent sinkings of many cargo ships. It would be of great help
                    in my work here if your answer were delivered through me.<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d593-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d593-f1" n="9" xml:id="d593-f1-content">
                <p>Adm. Nikolay Gerasimovich Kuznetsov.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d593-f2" n="10" xml:id="d593-f2-content">
                <p>No reply to this communication has been found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
